  "final_message": "`POST /orders` now accepts an optional `couponCode` string. The order stores it, and the `OrderPlaced` event includes it. The existing 39 tests pass and `npm run arch` reports no new violations. I didn't add tests for `couponCode` itself, so the new field is untested.\n\n- **Parsing** (`src/api/requestParsing.ts`): `couponCode` is read as an optional string. A non-string value returns 400.\n- **Validation** (`src/core/order.ts`): if present, it must be non-blank and at most 64 characters, otherwise 400. I chose the 64-character limit myself (`LIMITS.maxCouponCodeLength`), so change it if coupons can be longer.\n- **Order and event**: `Order` and `NewOrder` have the optional field, and `createOrder` only sets it when it's provided. `OrderPlaced` includes it the same way, so orders without a coupon produce exactly the same event as before.\n- **Event schema version**: I left `schemaVersion` at 3, because an optional field doesn't break existing consumers. Bump it if your team versions on any field addition.\n- **Not changed**: I didn't touch the `201` response body, which still returns `{ id, status, placedAt, currency, totalCents, lines }` as documented in `CLAUDE.md`. I also didn't change the persistence adapters or the docs.",
